## Found by the fm-5wq.14 corpus sweep (6b8315b6, 2026-09-24)

Seven scenes fail with ValueError: surface construction exceeds its 65536-point aggregate UV-grid budget:
- _2025/laplace/{derivatives.py MoveAroundPolesSeeDynamics, ShowSolutionPoles; integration.py SimplePole; main_equations.py SimplePolesOverImaginaryLine, ZetaFunctionPlot; main_supplements.py PreviewAnalyticContinuation}. All go through integration.py get_complex_graph with resolution=(301, 301), which is 90,601 points.
- _2026/print_gallery/exponential.py CreatePiHouseLog: Square3D(resolution=(1000, 1000)).

The Reference has no such cap.

Authored grid sizes across the pinned 3b1b/videos tree (resolution=(u, v) literals):
- up to 101x201 (20,301): the overwhelming majority;
- 201x201 (40,401): 2 sites;
- 250x250: 1 site;
- 301x301 (90,601): 5 sites;
- 501x501 (251,001): 1 site;
- 1000x1000 and 1001x1001: 1 site each.

## Where the cap lives
The cap is the shared sampling budget, not a surface-specific one:
- fmn_library::SamplingBudget::DEFAULT (graphs.rs DEFAULT_MAX_SAMPLES = 65_536);
- fmn-mobject surface_grid.rs MAX_SURFACE_GRID_POINTS;
- fmn-python portal_surface.rs;
- the Python mirrors surface_admission.py _MAX_SAMPLES, surface_alignment.py, surface_geometry.py and surface_mesh.py _BUDGET.

## Work
Give UV surfaces their own budget, sized from the data above (2^18 = 262,144 admits every authored grid except the two 1000x1000 outliers). Keep it a DoS bound: memory for a surface record is about 52 B/point before triangulation. Change every mirror consistently, and keep graph/field/streamline budgets where they are.

## Acceptance
- A 301x301 ParametricSurface constructs, aligns (Transform), meshes and renders in the portal.
- A grid over the new budget still refuses by name.
- A re-sweep moves the six laplace scenes off this error with no scene leaving ok.

