description:
Found while running PG-7 for fm-typeset-cache-preflight-wiring-1sn0.

At 29233ca6 the PG-7 producer's two formula workloads time the engine's bounded memory front, not what they name:
- formula-cold, documented as "cache-disabled layout";
- formula-cached, documented as "verified exact-key hit" from the store.

Since 472a19c0 (2026-09-20), TexEngine::typeset serves a repeated source from its per-engine memory LRU. Both producers call typeset_formula() on one engine:
- formula-cold calls it 1 (prime) + 3 (warm-up) + 24 (samples) times, so all 24 samples are memory hits;
- formula-cached primes via preflight and then samples the same engine, so its samples are memory hits as well, never the disk store.

Observed with the release-perf producer (scratch dump of measure_pg7, unqualified host, load ~2-5 on 128 threads):
- formula-cold median 1.7 us (min 1.6, max 1.8), 24/24 valid;
- formula-cached median 1.7 us (min 1.6, max 1.8), cache exact-key-miss -> exact-key-hit;
- text-10k-glyph median 2501 us (min 2201, max 3568).

A 1.7 us "cold layout" cannot be a layout: the same engine's front-door preflight lays the formula sheet out at ~3-6 ms per formula. As built, PG-7 formula-cold and formula-cached would pass their < 3 ms / < 100 us targets trivially. That makes them a gate that cannot fail on the workload it names.

Fix direction (a gate STRENGTHENING; meet the evidence standard in AGENTS.md):
- formula-cold times a layout with the memory front bypassed: a fresh engine per sample outside the timed region, or an engine-level memory-front-off option;
- formula-cached times a verified disk hit with a cold memory front: a fresh engine bound to the primed store, or memory front cleared per sample;
- re-derive the locked definitions/digests, and publish before/after numbers.
Do not reuse any PG-7 observation produced between 472a19c0 and the fix.

